WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.334
Alina Polyakova,

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.702
president and CEO of the Center

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.304
for European Policy Analysis.

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:04.738
She has done

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.172
extensive reporting on Putin

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.774
and his inner circle.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.609
So, Alina, I'm glad to have you back.

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:10.543
You know, we just played

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.711
that sound a moment ago

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.413
from Putin's alleged girlfriend, mother

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.547
of multiple of his children.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:17.117
And I want to play it again

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.485
emotional now.

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:19.085
But honestly,

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:20.420
looking information work

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.421
under the conditions

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.856
that we are currently living

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:24.891
and as we fight for our country

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.693
is like a weapon of war.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.261
And in terms of significance,

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:28.795
it holds

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.797
no less value than a Kalashnikov.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.432
Kalashnikov.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.302
What is she really saying here?

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.738
Well, I think a few things.

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.673
One, the whole idea

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.308
that information warfare

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:44.010
or the use of disinformation

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.111
is part and parcel

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.280
of how Russia engages in war.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.715
It's not just about the tanks.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.717
It's not just about the Kalashnikovs,

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:51.451
as she says.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.953
It's also about skewing the narrative

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.889
and skewing the very idea

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.023
of what's happening

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.625
in Russia's war against Ukraine.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.126
This is nothing new.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.261
She's really reconfirming

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.363
what has been official Kremlin policy.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.799
I think the second takeaway here

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.667
is something that she alludes to,

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.501
which is, of course,

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:11.538
that we are looking at almost a year

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:12.272
since Russia's

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.307
full scale invasion of Ukraine.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.241
And I think she says

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.409
at the beginning that

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.544
now we need this win,

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:19.079
something along those lines.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.180
And what she is really saying

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.181
there is this war

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.215
for Russia, the war

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:22.982
the Russia

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:25.018
of Putin have launched against Ukraine

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:27.420
is really an existential war for Putin

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.822
and for Russia itself.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.156
And many Russians

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.425
today inside of Russia do believe

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:35.762
that this is a war that they have to win.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.030
It's a nationalist war.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.999
They believe wrongly, of course, that Mr.

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.634
Putin is protecting them.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.102
And, Alina,

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:43.203
for anyone who had hoped that

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:44.838
maybe she would have

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:45.438
I don't know,

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.439
turned sides

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.241
or just decided to remain in Switzerland,

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:48.608
you know,

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.143
this obviously shows that's not the case.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.644
It took a long time for the United States

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.346
to put any sanctions on her whatsoever.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:54.147
They finally did

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.448
they thought it would make,

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:58.051
you know, too incendiary to Putin,

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:00.053
but she is now sanctioned.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.621
How influential is she?

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.356
Does she does she carry much sway?

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.524
Obviously,

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:05.291
We know who

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.694
she seems to be vis a vis him.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:08.761
And then along with that,

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:09.796
she got these titles,

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.731
you know, like head of some of these

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:13.633
crucial media companies.

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:16.169
Well, to be clear, she

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:18.004
is definitely a known name in Russia.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:19.105
I mean, she's Putin's

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.073
girlfriend, mistress,

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.207
whatever you want to call her,

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.408
or for that reason,

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:23.409
whatever she says

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.310
does get reported

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.012
in the Russian tabloids.

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.380
But in terms of having

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.283
political influence, she really doesn't.

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:33.052
I mean, she is here basically

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.988
reframing,

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:36.356
repeating what is a Kremlin

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:37.857
talking point.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.792
But she is a recognizable name.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:40.293
Of course,

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.295
the sanctions have probably forced her

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.197
to go back to Russia and leave

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:44.764
what we believe

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.199
was the very opulent lifestyle.

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:48.234
She was living in Switzerland,

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.636
where she now

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:51.237
is the chair of this new media group.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.239
But everyone knows inside of Russia

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.841
that she's only there

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:55.842
because she is

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.310
the mother of Putin's children.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.245
So she gets paid millions of dollars

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.213
for basically doing

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.114
absolutely nothing

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:02.248
except making

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.350
a few PR appearances here and there.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:04.951
Amazing.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.352
All right, Alina, thank you very much.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.520
Good to see you again. And thanks.

